# Where the pinned InterUSS automated-testing interface files in
# api/standards/interuss/ come from (docs/PLAN.md D13, §6.4; brief WP-21;
# E-03). Each file is a byte-for-byte copy of the file at `path` in
# interuss/automated_testing_interfaces at `commit`, kept at the same
# relative path so that the files' own relative references resolve.
# scripts/check-standards.sh checks every `sha256` offline;
# scripts/fetch-standards.sh -interuss re-fetches `url`. CI never fetches.
#
# The commit is the one the lab's pinned uss_qualifier reads the
# interfaces at (uspace-lab conformance/uss_qualifier/SOURCE: InterUSS
# monitoring v0.36.0, 0fabe238ef177f66266eba6048545ae1e6bbb4a0). Observed
# 2026-10-13: monitoring's uv.lock at that commit pins uas-standards 4.4.0;
# interuss/uas_standards tag v4.4.0 is 6e182f43ec960b3bccf131c9006ff9979dd8a56e
# (the same uas_standards commit as api/standards/SOURCE) and its
# submodule interfaces/interuss/automated_testing is 17502448f450fd9d923577c0667b7d4cb4812620;
# uss_qualifier's wire types come from that package. The monitoring
# repository's own submodule interfaces/automated_testing is at
# 3e6060bd6d5cd665eb5cc60ec7aaeab104547769, an older commit
# (flight_planning 0.5.0, injection 0.5.1 with two descriptions shorter);
# it is documentation in that repository and not what the suite imports.
# uspace-authority pins observation.yaml and commons.yaml at the same
# 17502448f450fd9d923577c0667b7d4cb4812620 (api/clients/SOURCE).
#
# The scope of each operation is in the file's `security` block (Q17:
# the file wins); internal/testif reads them from these copies in a test.
#
# scd v1 (scd/v1/scd.yaml, scope utm.inject_test_data) is NOT pinned and
# not built: at the pinned commit the F3548 suite drives flight_planning
# v1 (lab coverage.yaml, f3548-scd.yaml). A later lab pin that needs it
# adds it here with its own run (brief WP-21, scd v1).
#
# The generated code is internal/stdapi/interuss/<package>/<file>.gen.go
# (scripts/generate-interuss.sh, oapi-codegen at the go.mod tool pin, the
# configurations oapi-codegen.<package>[.<side>].yaml beside this file).

